Join us and work with global teams to support global customers ! At Arabelle Solutions, we have team members of more than 49 nationalities spread across 16 countries.

At Arabelle Solutions, we know diversity makes teams and business stronger.

### About Us

Arabelle Solutions is a leading provider of nuclear turbine island technology and services. A third of the world's nuclear power plants rely on our technologies and services.

Our innovative solutions and highly skilled teams energize the world with reliable, low-carbon electricity - critical for a sustainable future.

With a heritage going back to the industry's early days, our expertise is built on continuous design innovation, manufacturing world-class turbine island technology and providing essential services to maintain, maximize and extend the lifetime of nuclear power plants across  Europe, Asia and Africa.

Our technologies range from the world's most powerful steam turbine in operation to modular designs optimized for SMRs, as well as generators, pumps, heat-exchangers, controls systems and cyber security.

Arabelle Solutions has around 3,300 employees working across 16 countries.

# Product Manager - Networking

#### Manchester, M27 8SB

Apply now

We have fantastic opportunity for an experienced Product Manager to join our Networking Division

Salary
:   Up to £35,000 p/a + commission

Experience
:   Networking product knowledge

Location
:   Manchester

Department
:   Business Management - Networking

Job Reference
:   22-26

Closing Date
:   Fri, 25 Sep 2026

**Job Title: Product Manager AV**

**Salary:** Up to £35,000 + commission 

**Benefits:** Hybrid Working | PRP | LTS Income Protection |Medical Cash Plan | Life Assurance | Birthday Day Off | Salary Sacrifice - Pension, Share Incentive Plan, Electric Vehicle and Cycle to Work schemes | Free onsite parking and more

**About the Role**

To drive our vendor partners to increase sales, GP, GP% and market share in their given market.  This will be completed with strong communication and negotiations with the vendor at all levels while advising and promoting the products to our internal channel sales team and our customers.

**What you will be doing in this role**

**Profit and Working Capital Management – In line with reports produced by the Business Support Team**

* ​Use available management information to scrutinise relevant brand performance versus plan and act to correct or improve performance where necessary;
* Review pricing rules within the company’s ERP database to maximise our trading margin considering market conditions, stock availability and any special stock purchases that may have been made;
* Review daily the accounts-based data produced by the Accounts Department and take immediate and appropriate actions to remedy any issues that negatively affect the margin;
* Review each week the margin reports issued from the Accounts Department and take immediate and appropriate actions to remedy any issues that negatively affect the margin;
* Review aged and problematic stock during each month and take appropriate remedial action for the most cost-effective solution ensuring that the aged stock and working capital needs of the business are met raising any issues with the relevant Divisional or Business Manager;
* Proactively manage the stock profile targets and maintain a regular dialogue with the Divisional or Business Manager;
* Manage all stocking deals for the vendor.  Work with sales and marketing on a sales out plan before gaining sign-off.  Operate on a 0-3-month review cycle on all deals outside of standard stocking and cash flow terms;
* ​Proposes cost reductions and improved processes in respect of the administration involved with designated vendors.

**Vendor Relationships**

* **​**Develop an intimate understanding of the key trading terms for each of the division’s vendors; working to continually improve on them
* ​Develop a strong and close partnership with all divisional vendors;
* Provide support to accounts to chase vendors for prompt resolution to outstanding debit notes as per the report issued from the Vendor Claims team;
* Maintain or increase the market share for each vendor (measured by aggregate gross profit earned if possible) GP allowing.

**Business Development**

* **​**Help build short and long-term business plans in conjunction with the Divisional or Business Manager and, after sign off from the Board, help build strategies to achieve the agreed goals;
* Gain regular feedback from sales teams, vendors and other sources on market and competitive activity and reports this to the Divisional or Business Manager as required;
* Review and scrutinise daily quote reports.​Use this information to engage directly with customers and be forward thinking around stock forecasting and remedying any pricing issues before they happen;
* Review and minimise allocated stock for your area;
* Manage both sales and vendors pipeline via Pipedrive.​Use this information to formulate a successful buying plan;
* Develop sound technical product and market knowledge with the ability to demonstrate products directly to customers and end users;
* Implement marketing activities as required, and provide direction to the Product Marketing Manager that are in line with the divisional objectives and strategies;
* Provide feedback to the Divisional or Business Manager and Board on new vendor and product opportunities;
* Analysis of sell out data to identify opportunities and areas for improvement and implements appropriate action plans.​In conjunction with reports provided by the Business Administration Team.

**​****Internal Business Support**

* **​**Maintain face to face contact with our sales staff to ensure a desired level of vendor focus and where appropriate provide briefings to highlight key opportunities or other significant messages;
* Support the sales team with product and price queries and information required for customer proposals;
* Implement and drive internal and external sales activities and incentives that are in line with the Division’s and vendors’ goals;
* Organise appropriate training to maximise sales, profit and market share;
* Liaise with and support the customer services and Logistics teams to resolve any customer returns or returns stock issues escalating any major issues to the Divisional or Business Manager;
* Present to the Divisional or Business Manager or board as required on any issues that may affect any divisional vendor;
* Observe Company ground rules and procedures in respect of training and incentives;
* Provide feedback each month to the Divisional or Business Manager on any queries relating to the monthly management accounts;
* Identify key resellers and work with the sales specialists to maximize the business opportunities with in a target list of customers;
* Be the principle contact for the divisional vendor(s).

**What you will bring to the role**

**Essential Experience & Skills**

* Previous experience witihin the channel sales sector (IT/Telecom/AV/Networking)
* Previous experience of sales pipeline management
* Previous experience and/or understanding of supplier negotiations
* Technical acumen with the ability to understand and explain technical products to a non technical audience
* Ability to assess and analyse data such as sales run rates alongside sales pipelines and upcoming projects/tenders to ensure accurate product order management/stock levels
* Excellent excel skills and forecasting
* Planning and Organisation skills
* Commercial and business awareness

**​****Interested?**

***Nimans is part of the Midwich Group. We an equal opportunity employer and welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you meet the requirements of the role and are interested in this opportunity, please submit your CV for consideration.***

*All candidates must have the right to work in the UK.*

*Please note all roles that move to offer are subject to receipt of satisfactory references.*

*We have the right to close this vacancy early if we receive sufficient applications for the role. Therefore, if you are interested, please submit your application as early as possible.*

# Paid Search Manager

